  "text": "Skip to content\nLocal preview\nDraft content · 9 October 2026\nartifactory.\nMenu\nArtiSense\nTechnology\nHome\nProjects\nArtiSense\nTechnology\n\nARTISENSE / TECHNOLOGY\n\nA system designed around light.\n\nArtiSense is a chemical-sensing research project. Its proposed architecture connects photonic components with signal interpretation; the components below describe a system concept, not a validated device.\n\nON THIS PAGE\n01\nThe proposed signal path\n02\nPhotonics and signal interpretation\n03\nWhat integration needs to resolve\n04\nWhere AIFIELD contributes\nARTISENSE / 01\nPHOTONICS\nSIGNAL\nLIGHT\nConceptual illustration · not a product image or measured result\nThe proposed signal path\n\nVisible or infrared light interacts with a sample. The resulting optical response is detected and compared with a reference. Interpretation then seeks to connect changes in the spectrum with chemical information.\n\n01\nIlluminate\n\nIntroduce light under controlled conditions.\n\n02\nInteract\n\nObserve how the sample changes the optical response.\n\n03\nDetect\n\nCapture a signal suitable for reference comparison.\n\n04\nInterpret\n\nEvaluate spectral information within a calibration model.\n\nPhotonics and signal interpretation\n\nThe reviewed architecture describes a proposed reprogrammable analog neuromorphic processor, software support and connectivity. These are architectural directions. The supplied context does not establish which blocks have been implemented or integrated.\n\ni\n\nThe proposed ArtiSense analog processor is distinct from AIFIELD’s research into neural prediction of optical fields.\n\nWhat integration needs to resolve\nCalibration\n\nDefine the reference, operating conditions and sensitivity to variations in the sample.\n\nOptical coupling\n\nCharacterize the path between the light source, sample and detector in a physical setup.\n\nSystem constraints\n\nEstablish power, packaging, stability and signal-processing requirements through experiments.\n\nWhere AIFIELD contributes\n\nThe supplied material includes a photonic glucose chip-design example associated with this sensing direction. AIFIELD pages explain the design activity; ArtiSense validation pages explain what must be established by measurement. A simulated design is one input to that work.\n\nDesign & simulation\nCONTINUE EXPLORING\nApplications\nResearch & validation\nInvestors\n\nTHE NEXT CONVERSATION\n\nLet’s explore what\ncomes next.\n\nInvest in the company. Explore the science. Bring a question worth working on.\n\nDiscuss an investment\nExplore partnerships\nartifactory.\n\nEngineering light. Creating possibility.\n\nSensing technology and tools for designing photonic systems.\nProjects\nAll projects\nArtiSense\nAIFIELD\nCompany\nHome\nInvestors\nOur approach\nAbout\nPartnerships\nGet in touch\ninfo@artifactory.tech\nContact\nPrivacy\nArtifactory · 2026\nLocal review edition. Content and Polish translations await owner review.\nBack to top ↑",
